The reviewer-authored mutation is discriminating: for satisfying inputs `"010"` and `"110"`, the correct result is `"100"` while the mutated destination was `"101"`; `kprove` parsed and ran it, then exited 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState` showing the residual `"100"`. I found no material soundness or adequacy gap, so I’m assembling the seven-stage report and trust ledger with a `PASS / LEGIT` conclusion.
